# These files are redistributed byte-for-byte under their upstream licences, and
# CREDITS.md says so. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout would rewrite
# every LF in them, which both breaks that claim and trips the size guard in
# fetch.py -- it compares the bytes on disk against the size Commons reports, so
# a translated checkout looks like a tampered file. -text pins them.
*.svg -text
